.SH ERRORS
.SS cbor::structs<T>::encode
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]no_buffer_space\f[R]: a \f[CR]std::span<char>\f[R] that is too
small for the bytes.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]value_too_large\f[R]: the size of the bytes does not fit in
\f[CR]std::size_t\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
An error of the writer: \f[CR]no_buffer_space\f[R],
\f[CR]value_too_large\f[R], \f[CR]not_enough_memory\f[R] or
\f[CR]io_error\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
A \f[CR]std::chrono::year_month_day\f[R] that is no valid date throws
\f[CR]std::logic_error\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
A refused allocation of the result throws \f[CR]std::bad_alloc\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
A type that \f[CR]structs\f[R] does not take does not compile (types).
.SS cbor::structs<T>::decode
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]incorrect_type\f[R]: an item of another type, a missing or other
tag.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]number_out_of_range\f[R]: a number that the type cannot hold.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]key_not_found\f[R]: no key for a member that is not
\f[CR]std::optional\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]duplicate_key\f[R]: a key that comes twice.
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]too_little_data\f[R]: the input ends inside the item.
A byte after the item is not read.
\f[CR]not_enough_memory\f[R]: a refused allocation.
.IP \(bu 2
A null or empty owner throws \f[CR]std::logic_error\f[R].
.SS cbor::describe_members
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]decode\f[R] gives \f[CR]incorrect_type\f[R] for a missing tag or
another tag.
.IP \(bu 2
A description does not compile when it lists a member twice, gives two
members one key, names a member of another class, or has no
\f[CR]tag\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
A tag of a standard type or an invalid tag does not compile.
.IP \(bu 2
With reflection, a list that differs from the public data members does
not compile.
An annotation on \f[CR]T\f[R] does not compile.
.SS cbor::member
A pointer to a static member or to a member function does not compile.
A \f[CR]bool\f[R] or a character type as the key does not compile.
.SS CBOR_MEMBER
As member.
.SS Member types
\f[CR]decode\f[R] gives \f[CR]incorrect_type\f[R] for another item: a
\f[CR]std::vector<int>\f[R] takes a typed array, not an array.
An enum with no fixed underlying type, a \f[CR]long double\f[R] and a
struct under \f[CR]tagged_item\f[R] do not compile.
.SH NOTES
.SS cbor::structs<T>::encode
O(i + n): i items, n bytes.
The first form allocates one \f[CR]std::string\f[R].
A container target grows by O(n).
A span that holds the bytes allocates nothing.
A span that is too small and a writer use a temporary of O(n).
.SS cbor::structs<T>::decode
Common O(n); O((n/d)\(had) with tag 29.
The first form allocates the owner.
Every form allocates the containers of the result.
.SS cbor::describe_members
None at run time.
The checks run where \f[CR]encode\f[R] or \f[CR]decode\f[R] compiles.
.SS cbor::member
None at run time.
.SS CBOR_MEMBER
None at run time.
.SS Member types
As encode and decode.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS cbor::structs<T>::encode
.IP
.EX
\f[B]struct\f[R] person {
    std::string name;
    int age;
};
\f[B]auto\f[R] const bytes = cbor::structs<person>::encode(person{\(dqann\(dq, 30});
\f[B]if\f[R] (bytes)
    use(*bytes);   \f[I]// {\(dqage\(dq: 30, \(dqname\(dq: \(dqann\(dq}\f[R]
.EE
.SS cbor::structs<T>::decode
.IP
.EX
\f[I]// bytes: a std::string with {\(dqname\(dq: \(dqann\(dq, \(dqage\(dq: 30}\f[R]
\f[B]auto\f[R] const p = cbor::structs<person>::decode(std::move(bytes));
\f[B]if\f[R] (p)
    use((*p)\->age);   \f[I]// 30\f[R]
.EE
.SS cbor::describe_members
.IP
.EX
\f[B]template\f[R] <>
\f[B]struct\f[R] cbor::describe_members<header> {
    static \f[B]constexpr\f[R] std::optional<cbor::tag> tag = cbor::tag{160060};
    static \f[B]constexpr\f[R] std::tuple members{
        cbor::member{\(dqcontent\-type\(dq, &header::content_type},
    };
};
cbor::structs<header>::encode(header{\(dqtext/plain\(dq});   \f[I]// 160060({\(dqcontent\-type\(dq: \(dqtext/plain\(dq})\f[R]
.EE
.PP
\f[CR]CBOR_DEFINE_TYPE(T, TAG, members...)\f[R] writes this
specialization:
.IP
.EX
CBOR_DEFINE_TYPE(trailer, cbor::tag{160061}, cbor::member{\(dqchecksum\(dq, &trailer::checksum});
cbor::structs<trailer>::encode(trailer{7});   \f[I]// 160061({\(dqchecksum\(dq: 7})\f[R]
.EE
.PP
The macro stands at global scope.
A type whose name holds a comma goes through an alias.
.SS cbor::member
.IP
.EX
\f[B]template\f[R] <>
\f[B]struct\f[R] cbor::describe_members<senml> {
    static \f[B]constexpr\f[R] std::optional<cbor::tag> tag = cbor::untagged;
    static \f[B]constexpr\f[R] std::tuple members{
        cbor::member{0, &senml::n},
        cbor::member{2, &senml::v},
    };
};
cbor::structs<senml>::encode(senml{\(dqt\(dq, 1.5});   \f[I]// {0: \(dqt\(dq, 2: 1.5}\f[R]
.EE
.SS CBOR_MEMBER
.IP
.EX
\f[B]template\f[R] <>
\f[B]struct\f[R] cbor::describe_members<account> {
    static \f[B]constexpr\f[R] std::optional<cbor::tag> tag = cbor::untagged;
    static \f[B]constexpr\f[R] std::tuple members{
        CBOR_MEMBER(account, user),
        CBOR_MEMBER(account, level),
    };
};
cbor::structs<account>::encode(account{\(dqann\(dq, 2});   \f[I]// {\(dquser\(dq: \(dqann\(dq, \(dqlevel\(dq: 2}\f[R]
.EE
.SS Member types
.IP
.EX
\f[B]struct\f[R] reading {
    std::uint8_t id;
    std::optional<std::uint8_t> unit;
};
cbor::structs<reading>::encode(reading{4, std::nullopt});   \f[I]// {\(dqid\(dq: 4}\f[R]
cbor::structs<std::set<std::uint8_t>>::encode({3, 1});       \f[I]// 258([1, 3])\f[R]
.EE
